(PRC-51 — a non-blocking reap of a child that has already finished returns
 that child's PID with the error flag clear, in both the `reap child` and
 `reap process` spellings.
 The 300-millisecond wait is a margin for the child to exit, not a claim
 about scheduling; PRC-50 covers the still-running case.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-51.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   reap child without waiting returned the pid
   exit code 4
   reap process without waiting returned the pid
   exit code 6
)
a number called 'the first child' is fork the process.
If 'the first child' is 0 then, Exit 4.
Wait 300 milliseconds.
a number called 'polled by child' is reap child 'the first child' without waiting.
On error print "the non-blocking reap set the error flag".
If 'polled by child' is 'the first child' then, print "reap child without waiting returned the pid".
print "exit code {the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256}".
a number called 'the second child' is fork the process.
If 'the second child' is 0 then, Exit 6.
Wait 300 milliseconds.
a number called 'polled by process' is reap process 'the second child' without waiting.
If 'polled by process' is 'the second child' then, print "reap process without waiting returned the pid".
print "exit code {the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256}".
